WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
In December 2024, the Fed set a new target

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.670
range for its key interest rate:

3
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.520
four and a quarter to
four and a half percent.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.570
Rates on car loans, credit cards
and business loans follow it.

5
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.820
Yet the Fed doesn't set
the rate on a single

6
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.290
one of those loans.

7
00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.520
So if the Fed can't order
banks to charge more,

8
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.600
how does it push interest
rates up across the country?

9
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.610
In this mission, you'll open
the Fed's toolbox and meet

10
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.500
all four of its tools.

11
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.750
Then you'll compare two reserve markets,

12
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.960
the old system and today's,

13
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.250
and see what really moves the rate.

14
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.270
Your mission: find out how the
Fed really steers interest rates.
